From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:35:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: hm1092: Build on 7.3's subdev pad operations

v8 of the driver targets the media tree after 7.3, so two of its pad
operations need 7.3's form:

- .get_selection takes no struct v4l2_subdev_client_info on 7.3. The
  driver never reads it, so drop the parameter.
- .set_fmt is unset, relying on the subdev core falling back to .get_fmt,
  which arrived in 7.4-rc1 (48d8b2418f55 "media: v4l2-subdev: Always call
  get_fmt() if set_fmt() is unavailable"). On 7.3 VIDIOC_SUBDEV_S_FMT
  returns -ENOTTY instead and libcamera rejects the sensor, so point
  .set_fmt at v4l2_subdev_get_fmt, as fixed-format sensor drivers in 7.3
  do.

Drop this once the kernel moves past 7.3.

Signed-off-by: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hm1092.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hm1092.c
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hm1092.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hm1092.c
@@ -829,7 +829,6 @@
 }
 
 static int hm1092_get_selection(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
-				const struct v4l2_subdev_client_info *ci,
 				struct v4l2_subdev_state *state,
 				struct v4l2_subdev_selection *sel)
 {
@@ -870,6 +869,7 @@
 
 static const struct v4l2_subdev_pad_ops hm1092_pad_ops = {
 	.get_fmt = v4l2_subdev_get_fmt,
+	.set_fmt = v4l2_subdev_get_fmt,
 	.enum_mbus_code = hm1092_enum_mbus_code,
 	.enum_frame_size = hm1092_enum_frame_size,
 	.get_selection = hm1092_get_selection,
-- 
